{"metadata":{"symbolKind":"method","modules":[{"name":"AxiamSDK"}],"externalID":"s:8AxiamSDK0A6ClientC5closeyyYaKF","role":"symbol","title":"close()","roleHeading":"Instance Method","fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"close","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"() ","kind":"text"},{"text":"async","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"throws","kind":"keyword"}]},"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/axiamsdk\/axiamclient\/close()"]}],"abstract":[{"text":"Deterministic shutdown (CONTRACT.md §18).","type":"text"}],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"platforms":["Linux"],"tokens":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"close"},{"kind":"text","text":"() "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"async"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"throws"}],"languages":["swift"]}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"type":"heading","anchor":"discussion","level":2,"text":"Discussion"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Releases the HTTP client and its connection pool, and clears the cookie jar, the CSRF token","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"and any retained ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/Sensitive","isActive":true},{"text":" challenge token (§18.1 rule 6).","type":"text"}]},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Idempotent"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" (rule 2): calling it twice is a no-op the second time. Cleanup code runs","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"from error paths, and an error path that itself throws hides the original failure.","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Does not log out"}]},{"text":" (rule 5): it issues no request. The server-side session deliberately","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"outlives the client object — that is what lets a process restart and resume — so a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"close()"},{"text":" that logged out would silently end every user’s session on each deploy.","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Use after close is an error, not undefined"}]},{"type":"text","text":" (rule 4): every operation afterwards"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"throws "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/NetworkError"},{"type":"text","text":" naming the cause rather than silently reopening."}]}]}]},{"type":"aside","name":"Note","style":"note","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Swift’s ","type":"text"},{"code":"deinit","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" cannot ","type":"text"},{"code":"await","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", and releasing an ","type":"text"},{"code":"AsyncHTTPClient","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is async, so","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"this SDK cannot make deallocation a complete shutdown the way §18.1 rule 1’s “a ","type":"text"},{"code":"deinit","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"plus explicit "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"close()"},{"type":"text","text":"” suggests. "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"close()"},{"type":"text","text":" is therefore the only complete form, and is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"stated as required rather than implied."}],"type":"paragraph"}]}]}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK","doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/AxiamClient"]]},"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"minor":3,"major":0},"sections":[],"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/Axia